    "body": "## Motivation\n\nSGLang depends on the `ninja` package (`python/pyproject.toml`), but the JIT build runs a bare `ninja` from PATH (`kernels/jit/utils/compile/ninja.py`). The package puts its binary in the environment's scripts directory, which is only on PATH after activation. Running an environment without activating it, for example `/opt/venv/bin/python -m sglang.launch_server` from a service or a container entrypoint, fails on the first JIT build with `FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'ninja'`.\n\nThe Docker images are not affected because they install `ninja-build`. The Rust extension build already covers the same case by putting the interpreter's directory on PATH (`srt/rust_extensions/torch_build.py`).\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `toolchain.ninja_path()`: `ninja` on PATH, else the binary in `ninja.BIN_DIR`, else a `RuntimeError` naming both places, in the same shape as `hgcc_path()`.\n- `ninja.build()` runs that path instead of a bare `ninja`.\n- Three tests in `test/registered/unit/kernels/test_jit_cache.py`: the fallback, the error message, and `ninja.build()` with ninja missing from PATH.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot applicable, no kernel or model change.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe three new tests fail without the change (`toolchain` has no `ninja_path`, and `ninja.build()` raises `FileNotFoundError`) and pass with it. The rest of `test_jit_cache.py` gives the same results before and after.\n\nI ran this on Windows, where `sglang` itself does not import (`srt/utils/common.py` imports the Unix-only `resource`), so I loaded the modules with a local shim that skips the package `__init__` files and stubs `kernels/jit/utils/arch.py`. Tests that fail there for unrelated reasons (`tvm_ffi` and `fcntl` missing, Windows paths) fail the same way with and without the change. CI runs the file on Linux in `base-a-test-cpu`.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\npre-commit was not run locally; I kept to 88 columns and the existing import order.\n\ncc @DarkSharpness\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40890981532](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40890981532)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40890981368](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40890981368)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40890981322](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40890981322)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
